---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Privacy policy for the "Automate" LinkedIn developer app.
//
// LinkedIn's app-creation form requires a live privacy policy URL before the
// app can be created at all, same reason as the TikTok one at /tiktok/privacy:
// narrow and accurate to what this tool actually does, not a generic template.

const updated = '3 September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Automate (LinkedIn)"
  description="Privacy policy for Automate, a personal LinkedIn drafting tool."
>
  <main class="legal" id="main">
    <p class="eyebrow mono">AUTOMATE · LINKEDIN INTEGRATION</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated mono">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>What this covers</h2>
    <p>
      Automate is a private, single-operator tool used by May Abiodun to publish posts to
      her own LinkedIn profile. It is not offered to the public, has no user accounts, and
      is not used to process other people's data.
    </p>

    <h2>What it collects</h2>
    <p>When the operator connects her own LinkedIn account, the tool stores:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>an OAuth access token for that account;</li>
      <li>the account's LinkedIn member identifier, used to address the posting API;</li>
      <li>the text and, where used, a single image of each post it has published.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      That is the complete list. The tool does not read the account's connections, messages,
      feed, or any other person's information. It requests only the permissions needed to
      publish a post as the connected account (<code>openid</code>, <code>profile</code>,
      <code>w_member_social</code>).
    </p>

    <h2>What it does not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No data about other LinkedIn members.</li>
      <li>No advertising or tracking identifiers. The tool has no analytics.</li>
      <li>No payment information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>
      Tokens and post records are held in a private Postgres database hosted by Supabase,
      reachable only with a server-side secret key.
    </p>

    <h2>What is shared</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing is sold, and nothing is shared with third parties for their own purposes. Data
      moves only between the operator's own systems and LinkedIn's API in order to publish a
      post to the connected account.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      The token is kept only while the integration is in use. The operator can revoke the
      app's access at any time from LinkedIn's own settings, which invalidates the stored
      token immediately; the stored copy is then deleted. To request deletion of anything
      held by this tool, use the contact address below.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If the tool's behaviour changes, this page is updated before the change ships, so that
      what is described here stays true of what the app actually does.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href="mailto:silkvoice1214@gmail.com">silkvoice1214@gmail.com</a></p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.25rem 6rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    opacity: 0.6;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.8rem); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .updated { font-size: 0.78rem; opacity: 0.6; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 0.6rem; }
  .legal ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .legal code { font-size: 0.9em; opacity: 0.85; }
</style>
